{"event_type":"review","id":"5ed0e92ccbb8b8198a256bff862999a65d51d13bbe383c8ae5da2058010859a9","occurred_at":"2026-11-17T22:27:56Z","payload":{"artifacts":[{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/45bf87ca765cefb04985caa8bb44c05c95945cba415068851daee970ce91e49a","sha256":"45bf87ca765cefb04985caa8bb44c05c95945cba415068851daee970ce91e49a"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/ea694509f4e05d05edea7cf64b739cbd4cfc6b147a5e2c182895cde65a6245a7","sha256":"ea694509f4e05d05edea7cf64b739cbd4cfc6b147a5e2c182895cde65a6245a7"},{"kind":"git-bundle","location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/d5615911bef6f24f79a560c3a38ab524e4155af3637070be2107e0197e53cb61","sha256":"d5615911bef6f24f79a560c3a38ab524e4155af3637070be2107e0197e53cb61"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/0e250d25650c833f3d9b2e2fb2500ae1036be09dd0c886300902941cb0a0fa50","sha256":"0e250d25650c833f3d9b2e2fb2500ae1036be09dd0c886300902941cb0a0fa50"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/f404bb8912f0dd84bf28fe1a4782547708c6dcfcbb2c917ca65f4767a529ef9f","sha256":"f404bb8912f0dd84bf28fe1a4782547708c6dcfcbb2c917ca65f4767a529ef9f"}],"attempt_id":"6d21fed8ed18d2ffd2ff366b8f659c1e9df6858bedd585fccf8ea15502b4e82a:0:1","base":"c602697669c0a99ecc4cccc9b644548d9f318ecc","completion":{"errors":[],"exit_code":0,"scope_verified":true,"skipped":false,"terminal":true},"findings":[{"anchor_status":"verified","blob":"be79c1bb605ff6a51e61d15be0d4bf546ce15a9e","body":"**Capture the worker dependencies before asserting header-failure isolation.**\n\n`f.boundDeps` stays empty in this test because this `makeReviewAddress` call does not install a capturing `workerFactory`. At test/ops/review/observation-wiring.test.ts:768, `every()` therefore always returns `true`.\n\nAdd the capturing factory used by `invoke`. Assert that `f.boundDeps.length` is greater than zero before checking `observationWriter`. The append-count assertion checks writes, not whether the worker received the writer.\n\nAs per path instructions, “Prefer assertions that exercise intended behavior and its failure modes”.","id":"c11de9a91c10b3109d09ed8f9ab37742d90e14a174266326854a8fbc4b903986","intervals":[[768,768]],"path":"test/ops/review/observation-wiring.test.ts","severity":"minor","source_id":null,"status":"untriaged","title":"Capture the worker dependencies before asserting header-failure isolation."},{"anchor_status":"verified","blob":"933895c565ecc6a1f5605bfd23d1d8bb620ff92d","body":"**The race test deadlocks instead of interleaving.**\n\n`removePrWorktree` enters the per-PR lock in `withAdmission` (`src/adapters/git/prWorktree.ts:117-118`) before it reaches the `worktree remove` call that `gatedRun` parks on. `resolvePrWorktree` uses the same lock, so it waits behind the parked removal. The test awaits that resolve at line 340. `removeGate.release()` runs only after that await, so the release never happens. The test body times out, and the removal stays parked with a dangling promise.\n\nThe overlap the test describes cannot occur under this lock. The resolve always runs after the removal finishes. To exercise the in-lock reload, the test should wait until the removal is parked inside the lock, start the resolve without awaiting it, release the gate, and then await the resolve. Update the assertions to expect the serialized order.","id":"10aa35954b615ef8e20b79cbe6f1b148a0b33150d98d3f30623cef1e223807ca","intervals":[[328,342]],"path":"test/ops/review/prWorktree.remove.test.ts","severity":"major","source_id":null,"status":"untriaged","title":"The race test deadlocks instead of interleaving."},{"anchor_status":"verified","blob":"933895c565ecc6a1f5605bfd23d1d8bb620ff92d","body":"**Port `mutexRegistry` to the `SlotWorktreeRegistry` contract.**\n\n`PrWorktreeOpts.registry` is typed `SlotWorktreeRegistry` (`src/adapters/git/prWorktree.ts:167`). `baseOpts` takes the same type (`test/ops/review/prWorktree.helpers.ts:341`). `mutexRegistry` returns a `WorktreeRegistry` object with `load`, `save`, `update(key, entry | null)` and `withLock` (`test/ops/review/prWorktree.remove.test.ts:176,186-227`). It has no `read` or `withPrLock`. The harness is passed to `baseOpts` at lines 247, 272, 279, 337 and 341.\n\nThe removal tail calls `opts.registry.read(opts.pr)` (`src/adapters/git/prWorktree.ts:776`). The resolver calls `opts.registry.withPrLock(...)` (`:118`). With this harness, `read` is undefined, so the call throws a `TypeError` before the test assertions run. The same member gap can also fail the type check at the `baseOpts` call sites.\n\nThe harness also stores the wrong values. When the entry matches the removed tree, production calls `opts.registry.update(opts.pr, { version: 1, state: 'unbound', incomplete: true })` (`src/adapters/git/prWorktree.ts:795`). The harness stores that value verbatim and does not delete the key. The assertions at lines 252, 299-308 and 347-351 expect the legacy `{ path, branch, createdAt }` shape and the `load@` and `update:<key>:null@` call labels. Production does not emit those labels.\n\nRebuild `mutexRegistry` on the `SlotWorktreeRegistry` members, including `read`, `withPrLock` and `update`. Keep the lock-depth recording and the `pauseNextSave` hook. Update the expected `calls` and stored entries to match the writes that production makes.","id":"6b36cf5c37fbd1b85328bd59ae9d8df64cc0c517c3f24caa7798e022eb32d03f","intervals":[[186,227]],"path":"test/ops/review/prWorktree.remove.test.ts","severity":"major","source_id":null,"status":"untriaged","title":"Port `mutexRegistry` to the `SlotWorktreeRegistry` contract."}],"head":"2e2c09eda2428834f49fab15ca3af608d78e2e7d","head_tree":"067d49da10942551a3c39da201ad1d79467f9afa","input_scope":[{"blob":"665c17d2db52d243a8a51c93e1f52a5a37153866","intervals":[[1,366]],"path":"test/ops/review/address.admission.test.ts"},{"blob":"cb2f3c7e93eeef4fce33ea51983addb4ea8b0e0c","intervals":[[1,4